  "notes": {
    "Josh.17.16": "The land-of-the-valley construction is compressed in LSG; the land noun is contextual, not a separate French lexical equivalent.",
    "Josh.18.8": "The travelers are referred to by a pronoun; the deictic 'here' refers to Shiloh and is implicit in the French destination.",
    "Josh.19.10": "Qualify both target ordinals in verse 11 explicitly. A bare ordinal after a comma defaults to verse 10.",
    "Josh.19.32": "Repeated addressee in Hebrew is expressed only once in French; initial occurrences attached contextually.",
    "Josh.19.47": "LSG preserves its own interpretation of the border construction; repeated Leshem is pronominal in the final clause.",
    "Josh.18.12–19": "Repeated 'the ends were' constructions are verbalized as aboutir: retain the smallest multi-unit translation group, while leaving repeated boundary nouns and implicit directional verbs contextual."
